      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sticking to a large spinach juice *every day* could indeed become your new baseline, but you must still monitor your INR closely with that new routine. While warfarin can adjust, sudden, concentrated increases in Vitamin K from a massive daily serving can still throw your blood clotting time off. Since your doctor gave a warning, it's safer to start with moderate additions and let your labs guide the adjustments, rather than assuming the drug will handle a major dietary spike.",
